# Spherical cap: open disk topology, a single circular boundary loop.
#
# The canonical parameterization input, which the example set otherwise lacked --
# LSCM, ARAP and OMT all require a boundary, and every other mesh here is either
# closed or has several boundary loops.
#
# It is also a *quantitative* curvature asset, because the answers are known in
# closed form. Cut from the unit sphere at radius 0.8, so cap height h = 1 - 0.6:
#   Gaussian curvature K = 1/R^2 = 1 everywhere
#   mean curvature H = 1/R = 1 everywhere
#   area = 2*pi*R*h = 2.5133
# Discrete estimators should converge to these under refinement.
#
# Curved, so a conformal map genuinely distorts area: good OMT input.
# Wound so normals point away from the sphere centre.

